    },
    "body": "**Problem:** The binary verifier counts signatures from expired and revoked keys toward `--min-good-sigs`.\r\nEnough of these signatures can satisfy the threshold without any active signing key, and they are returned as good signatures.\r\n\r\n**Fix:** Warn about expired and revoked signatures and exclude them before trust classification and threshold counting.\r\nThe focused test in `contrib/verify-binaries/test.py` covers inactive signatures alone and alongside an active signature.\r\n\r\nSignatures are excluded if GnuPG reports their keys as expired or revoked using the local keyring, even if they were created while those keys were active.\r\n\r\nThis was found and disclosed responsibly by the Red Team 🟥.",
